NNOOTTEESS
       For security reasons, ssuu always logs failed log-in attempts to the _b_t_m_p
       file, but it does not write to the _l_a_s_t_l_o_g file at all. This solution
       can be used to control ssuu behavior by PAM configuration. If you want to
       use the ppaamm__llaassttlloogg(8) module to print warning message about failed
       log-in attempts then ppaamm__llaassttlloogg(8) has to be configured to update the
       _l_a_s_t_l_o_g file as well. For example by:

          session required pam_lastlog.so nowtmp

